%% Report 6.5.1 Sequence Diagram, donation and proof recording
%% The central flow of the system. Deck slide 25.
%% Source of truth: server/src/services/payment.service.ts handleCallback(),
%% donation.service.ts recordBlockchainProof(), blockchain.service.ts
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Donor
    participant Client as React Client
    participant API as Express API
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Gateway as Payment Gateway
    participant Chain as Sepolia

    Donor->>Client: choose campaign, enter amount
    Client->>API: POST /payments/session
    API->>DB: insert payment_transaction (pending)
    API->>Gateway: request checkout / STK push
    Gateway-->>API: checkout token
    API-->>Client: session reference
    Client-->>Donor: waiting screen

    Gateway->>Donor: mobile money prompt
    Donor->>Gateway: authorise on handset

    Gateway->>API: POST /payments/callback
    API->>DB: find transaction by reference

    alt already marked success
        API-->>Gateway: 200, return existing donation
        Note over API: idempotent, a repeated<br/>callback creates nothing
    else pending, signature valid
        API->>DB: mark transaction success
        API->>DB: insert donation (receipt number)
        API->>DB: award impact points
        API-->>Gateway: 200 acknowledged
        Note over API,Chain: proof write is not awaited,<br/>the donor is never blocked on the chain
        API-)Chain: recordDonationProof(hash)
        Chain--)API: transaction hash
        API->>DB: update blockchain_record (confirmed)
    end

    Donor->>Client: open receipt
    Client->>API: GET /donations/:id
    API->>DB: read donation + proof
    API-->>Client: receipt, transaction hash
    Client-->>Donor: receipt with verifiable proof
